    {
      "id": "dc7a9f3e-ec29-4eac-8c9c-4fcc2a7b7435",
      "q_id": "SGD064",
      "index": "SGD OG Campus Living",
      "title": "Three students are discussing living on campus.The people at the accommodation office want to know who's coming back to live on campus next year. We've got to let them know for sure by next week. It sounds like most people are coming back. What are you guys going to do? Have you decided yet?Yeah, I have. I've decided to keep living on campus in the same place that I'm in now. I've already put my name down, actually. And so has Jake Jake, my roommate. I really like living here, mainly because I enjoy living with Jake. It's so easy, and we just get on really well. We seem to have the same idea about keeping things tidy, and we like each other's company. What about you both? What do you think you'll do next year?I'm pretty happy where I am, so I'm going to stay here, too. It's convenient. Everything's so close by, the library, the gym. And of course, there's zero travel time to get to class. I'm still late sometimes, though. The food isn't the best, and maybe that's one thing I'd change if I could. But it's no big deal, and it's easy being right here, so I won't leave until I absolutely have to.Yeah, I know what you mean. It's super convenient, but sometimes I feel like it's almost too easy. It's great here, but I'm at the point where I want to get out into the real world. I'm ready for that next stage of life to start. You know, become a bit more independent, meet some different people.But there are so many people here. That's why I like it. It's a very social atmosphere, don't you think? There's always someone around and something going on. It's really easy to meet people. I admit, though, I do like to eat off campus sometimes. The food here gets so boring after a while. But if I moved away, I'd miss all the friends I've made here.Is It's not very private, though, is it? I feel like everyone knows what everyone else is doing all the time. It's been good for the first year, don't get me wrong. It's given me a good start, and I've met some great people, like yourselves. But now I want to try something new, spread my wings a bit, and I want to get some life skills, manage my money and all that.Look, that's fair enough. But what's the rush? This stage of life is never going to come again. I've got no responsibilities except study, and that is all going to change in a couple of years. So I'm happy to wait until then to get out into the big wide world.",
